SUMMARY="A version control system of signed, commuting changes, with Git interop"
DESCRIPTION="oxy is the command line of Oxygen, a version control system built on \
patch theory: changes commute, conflicts are recorded rather than blocking, \
every change can be signed, and a trust policy says who may move what. It \
imports and exports Git history, clones from OxygenHub and other Oxygen \
hosts, and keeps repositories on disk or in S3, GCS or Azure buckets."
HOMEPAGE="https://oxygenhub.io/andymccall/oxygen"
COPYRIGHT="2026 Andy McCall"
LICENSE="MIT
	Apache v2"
REVISION="1"
